### They ask whether their child's attachment to them and reactions to other people are normal.

19 of 198 posts.

These posts ask about wanting one parent constantly, screaming at separation or strangers, rejecting a familiar adult, or a baby seeming unusually content without the parents. Children range from five weeks to almost two years. Some changes follow illness, hospital procedures, travel or daycare, while others begin suddenly with no clear explanation; parents ask when independence will return and whether the child has been frightened or developed an insecure attachment.

- "Everyone is telling me she’ll grow out of it, but she’ll be 2 in November and is still going strong. I can’t take her anywhere. I’ve tried so many times and she just looses it. When I try to soothe her nothing helps. She acts like she’s being mauled by a bear. Does anyone have any advice? I’m so burnt out, I feel so isolated." [sr055-0006]
