- "My 18mo daughter is giggling while I'm watching TV. I look back and her diaper is off. She has a toothbrush to her private parts (they play with toothbrushes,  mrs Rachels toothbrush song). Again, she is not abused. How do I know? I am with her/them 24/7." [sr082-0078]
- "[…] One thing that does take me back, is her excessive need to gnaw on my chest/shoulder. Whenever anyone holds her, she will open her mouth as wide as she can and go straight for their chest/shoukder, almost as if she is rooting for milk. She’ll do this even if she’s just nursed. And sometimes I’ll try to nurse her again to see if that’s it but she just gets fussy and doesn’t eat. […]" [sr095-0042]
