- "He recently started rolling onto his tummy at night but cannot roll back yet. He gets stuck and cries. We also get nervous because sometimes he sleeps face-down instead of turning his head properly, so we flip him back — but then he fully wakes up." [sr028-0128]
- "But for the last few nights she has been waking and fussing for her feed and when I look in her bassinet she has manoeuvred herself all the way to the side with her face pushed against it because she’s on her side. It is mesh so I suppose it’s breathable? […]" [sr046-0050]
- "It's gotten to the point where the skin in that spot is permanently damaged! Even when there wasn't a fall in a while, it's slightly discoloured and looks like scar tissue." [sr004-0081]
- "Is this normal? Did your baby bruise a lot when they became really mobile and started exploring the world?" [sr035-0049]
- "[…] I called the ambulance and we went to hospital and had a CT scan. We were told he had a stable left parietal lobe subarachnoid hemorrhage. He returned mostly to his normal self that evening and we were discharged after one night. […]" [sr044-0148]

**But:** The injury post also reports reassuring hospital observations and an expected recovery, without providing that later outcome: "The pediatrician said it is very unlikely there will be any long term consequences but will follow him up in 3 months to check up. I am hoping to hear about similar incident where children have made a full recovery to help me with the anxiety of this incident." [sr044-0150]

