### The parent asks whether the child sleeps too much or needs a different amount from the guidance.

6 of 62 posts.

Parents ask whether long nights, multiple long naps or too little awake time are excessive, even when the child seems happy and active. Ages range from three months to fifteen months; some worry about missed feeds or time to practise walking, while one notices longer naps after sensory exercises but continued irritability.

- "For context, he’s a big boy. 28 lb 15 month old. He sleeps 13 hours a night, and then begs for a 2 hour morning nap. Around 3 he sleeps another 2 hours. Cries until he is put down. We’ve heard “teething” “growing” etc. but when is too much, too much?" [sr024-0019]
- "I know I shouldn’t complain about my baby sleeping but i’m starting to get concerned with the amount she sleeps during the day. Could this be a big growth spurt or should I be concerned that she is getting sick? Before this her naps were like an hour long max several times a day. She hasn’t been eating that well either. She will sometimes suck down a whole bottle and other times she will scream at it until she goes back to sleep, which causes her to miss the feed." [sr042-0114]
- "[…] She’s a normal, active baby, already trying to push herself around to crawl, talkative and smiley. Is it something I need to be worrying about? Should I be waking her up? […]" [sr049-0003]
- "Ive tried capping her naps but she is SO tired and angry during her wake window if she naps anything less than an hour and a half. I know it's early to have her on a two nap schedule but she was getting even less awake time on a three nap, we tried shorter naps more frequently and she struggled so hard! This seems to be her natural routine and she is thriving on this, just not awake her recommended 10 hours." [sr056-0091]
- "[…] I’m so relieved that she’s sleeping at last but I’m concerned about the duration and her irritability when awake. […]" [sr075-0103]

**But:** One parent reports a recent check finding the baby healthy and progressing. "She is genuinely the happiest baby. She’s gaining weight, 90th percentile. And she is meeting all her milestones except a long amount of tummy time which we are working on. She isn’t sick and we just went to the doctor and they said she has a clean bill of health." [sr094-0057]

