A ten-and-a-half-month-old abruptly refuses formula bottles and a cup after previously drinking them, while a four-to-six-month-old becomes harder to feed and stops opening the mouth for a bottle. The latter parent also reports a brief loss of grabbing, mouthing and rolling, then a return of those skills.

