## Pattern 1, share 04: across the yes posts

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 160 of 199 |
| others | 88 of 199 |
| bought | 2 of 199 |
| feeling | 124 of 199 |

### What they tried, in their words

The tag counts described actions already taken, including medical consultations and booked evaluations; plans alone do not count.

- "Nope he just suddenly slowly started, I stopped like trying to “quiz” him too and instead just would identify items as we played etc with no expectation of him “saying”something back and then slowly he just started doing it, but even now the majority is just gibberish of what he mimics back but it’s better than it was a few months ago so I know we are making progress" [sr021-0030]
- "She also does not use screens at all, and I stay at home with her and talk all the time. We do read 5-10 books a day and sing songs on repeat, I just feel like i’m missing something!" [sr018-0079]
- "It’s happened at the airport, restaurants, and the doctor’s office. I even brought the same fluffy changing mat covers that we use at home to make it feel familiar, but it made no difference." [sr046-0089]
- "She has started to develop a flat head on her right side. I've been trying to do stretches with her and turning her head to the left when she's sleeping but she turns it back within minutes." [sr127-0039]
- "I did take her to the pediatrician this week bc she’s been doing it so excessively the past few days & they checked her urine which was fine. They gave me some nystatin cream and powder to apply to her but we haven’t seen any changes." [sr122-0006]
- "Oh, one other point, toys. Don’t seem to work at all, he also refuses a paci, and I’m not comfortable with a mirror or toys that go on his car seat or the backseat as they are not approved by car seat experts." [sr017-0227]
- "Our home is very intentionally set up for him with toy rotations, baby proofed open spaces, play couch, etc." [sr089-0028]
- "Does any of this seem concerning? Am I overthinking it? He didn’t qualify for our state early intervention and they said I could reassess at 2 if I still wasn’t comfortable." [sr002-0203]
- "I’ve been giving Tylenol, puree popsicles, and lots of teething things to help with that" [sr057-0056]
- "However, I want to help my child in anyway. So I booked an evaluation 2 weeks from now, I was surprised I didn’t need a referral but I do have to pay out of pocket. Am I wrong for this? I know he could start to progress soon, but I am concerned." [sr112-0051]

### What other people told them or did

The tag covers reported advice or actions by adults, including clinicians, relatives, caregivers and online sources. Comparing children’s milestones alone does not count.

- "Our first born hit every milestone early, I know comparison is the thief of joy, and our pediatrician literally said “there’s nothing wrong with her, she’s just lazy” when I told him my concerns at our one year check in. But I can’t get this nagging feeling out of my head that something is wrong." [sr016-0134]
- "My 9 month old recently had her check up at the doctor, and when I was asked if she was trying to pull to stand, I told her no because she’s not, and the doctor got on to me and gave me a sheet of exercises and told me she needed to be walking at her 12 month check up." [sr028-0123]
- "I took her to my pediatrician who said it’s normal toddler behaviour but i am not convinced with his answer as my other friend child never did it" [sr050-0237]
- "I have mentioned it to our pediatrician and have been told it’s a normal behavior but my family is making me feel like it’s not." [sr027-0021]
- "her grandma taught her that hitting is a game or a joke (we live with her) & I ALWAYS said please don’t do that or when she’s older she’s going to be hitting for fun." [sr104-0011]
- "Thank you! I’ve never smacked her hand before, but that was the fourth hit she had given someone and at that point all the moms were like wtf? Why aren’t you correcting this? I was shocked with her behavior and also embarrassed" [sr104-0013]
- "I told my dad, and he thinks he’s too young to have a favourite. Personally, I think my dad is just upset that a boy likes pink." [sr035-0131]
- "Thank you for the great tips regarding pointing. I shall try that.. I’m a first time mom here.. I really didn’t know that pointing was such an important skill to learn for kids. I was concerned at 15 months when he was not responding consistently to his name. When I asked the pediatrician she said for early evaluation I need to wait unil 18 months. I wish I had started earlier.." [sr008-0018]
- "[…] Her pediatrician said they will evaluate her and decide if any further testing is needed." [sr060-0084]
- "Our kiddo is 7mo. Milestones always exacerbate my PPA and when she turned 7mo and wasn’t babbling, I got anxious. Calmed myself down - but two weeks later The Bump app mentioned that if kiddo “isn’t interested in babbling or mimicking sound yet, it’s a good idea to contact your pediatrician”" [sr046-0079]

### What they bought or paid for

Only two yes posts explicitly describe paid or insured care, or booking an evaluation with an out-of-pocket cost. These five excerpts come from those two posts; one also describes the older child’s care and quotes a conditional price. Possessing a toy or using an app does not by itself establish a purchase.

- "[…] We did start speech therapy last week just as a little extra push (it’s only 30 min so really I doubt it’s doing much but insurance covers it so why not). […]" [sr021-0029]
- "[…] My insurance won’t cover speech until 18 months anyway and my state EI is not free and quite honestly horrible quality for the cost, and I’m not convinced he’d qualify anyway due to his receptive language being appropriate. […]" [sr021-0026]
- "[…] It’s sliding scale based on income - so each session would be around 85 dollars for 30 minutes. […]" [sr021-0028]
- "[…] With my first we did 2 sessions before pulling her out for private where it was covered by insurance (EI isn’t covered so that would’ve been all out of pocket). […]" [sr021-0028]
- "[…] So I booked an evaluation 2 weeks from now, I was surprised I didn’t need a referral but I do have to pay out of pocket. […]" [sr112-0051]

### How they say they feel

The tag counts the speaker’s stated feelings, including affection, curiosity and explicit lack of worry. A question asking whether to worry, or a description only of the child’s feelings, does not by itself count.

- "[…] I'm scared. I've been lacking in some areas due to PP anxiety and depression but now I feel like I completely fucked up my child's development. […]" [sr052-0064]
- "I thought it was teething, but gels and medicine that should have decreased the gum pain showed no change. I'm worried something's wrong and since I have the maternal instincts of a turnip, I won't recognize it." [sr010-0210]
- "My thing is she wasn’t hitting for fun, she was hitting to not share out of anger. Should I be worried she’s on the spectrum? I am seriously crying I just feel so bad she was SUCH a mean, misbehaved baby. She’s never been like this. I feel so embarrassed and sad and like I’m just a bad mom." [sr104-0012]
- "We were referred to neuro, with the appointment tomorrow, but after reading a lot this last couple of months I’m sure she’s going to be diagnosed with CP, and I’m devastated." [sr128-0032]
- "I feel abandoned by my mom at a time I needed her the most. Things are tough right now." [sr102-0106]
- "Not sure if it’s a phase but my three month old cries big time pretty much every time I set her down and step away for a few minutes which is \~exhausting\~. I love the cuddles but it makes it hard to get anything else done throughout the day. The one good thing is that when I shower she tolerates being in the bouncer and watching me through the glass but otherwise it’s a no go." [sr095-0079]
- "I feel like I broke my baby 😭 idek what to do to help her its honestly heartbreaking to see her scared." [sr064-0015]
- "Now I am sitting here on day 2 after our outing completely terrified. Should I be concerned? I don’t know what to do." [sr004-0189]
- "The pediatrician is not concerned with his weight at all, so neither am I. […]" [sr022-0114]
- "I wasn't able to find anything about other kids who play for that long so I was curious if you guys had experience with kids like that." [sr123-0018]
- "Don't get me wrong! We love him so much and he can be quite a happy smiley baby but then he just gets so fussy for seemingly no reason.." [sr128-0011]
- "At first it was adorable and now we’re all overstimulated 24/7 and can’t catch a break! It doesn’t help that my mother thinks it’s incredibly abnormal and swore none of her babies did this." [sr128-0039]


