### The caregiver asks whether delayed sitting or an unusual way of getting around needs help.

8 of 198 posts.

Caregivers ask about babies who sit when placed but cannot get into sitting, do not crawl or pull up, or travel by rolling or army crawling. Most are around eight to eleven months, and one aunt describes a nephew approaching a year. They try floor time and moving toys out of reach, question whether weight or stronger language explains the difference, and seek encouragement alongside medical assessment.

- "My 10.5 month old isn't able to get into the sitting position from lying on her back. When put on her tummy she immediately rolls back to lying flat and only prefers to roll back on her right side. She's obviously not able to crawl or pull to stand. Though she's able to sit independently for longer period and can stand with support. She also slightly pulls herself to standing position when she's on my lap in front of sofa. When she's flat, she can come to sitting position by holding our finger." [sr002-0223]

- "My baby is really refusing to crawl! I've been putting toys slightly out of reach from him. He does that whole thing where he gets up on his hands and positions himself, but then he starts crying, plops down on the ground, rotates his body, and rolls. We've been doing this once or twice a day for the past week, and he just won't crawl! He'd rather plop and roll to the toys. If I move the toys when he rolls, he starts crying." [sr085-0123]

- "My 9 month old is army crawling, and he gets on his hands and knees and rocks back and forth. His 9 month WCC is soon and I’m not sure how to answer the question of “Is he crawling?”" [sr016-0027]

- "I am just wondering if this can really explain his motor delay. Did anyone have a similar situation? I think our pediatrician is way too chill and she gave us an appointment so late because she wanted to give him time to catch up, but honestly he doesn’t seem to be improving. I am thinking whether I should intervene." [sr058-0038]

- "Con casi 1 año el bebé está sentado y ya. No se desplaza ni se apoya. Yo he intentado alejar un poco sus juguetes de él pero por supuesto se frustra, llora... y el tummy time nada, no quiere hacer nada y llora." [sr041-0039]

**But:** An unusual crawl is not always accompanied by missing transitions or standing skills. "He gets from army crawling to sitting, sit to stand, cruises on furniture and occasionally does a few movements in 4 point crawl but then always ends up flopping down and commando crawling." [sr005-0194]

