### The caregiver worries that the child is not using their hands for expected tasks.

5 of 198 posts.

These posts concern purposeful reaching, holding a bottle, bringing objects to the mouth, stacking blocks or persisting with puzzles and sorters. The children range from three and a half months to almost 18 months, with different skills missing at different ages. Caregivers offer toys, model actions or ask whether an apparent skipped step counts as a delay.

- "My LO is almost 18 months old and she has always seemed to lack interest in most fine motor activities, such as stacking blocks, doing puzzles, shape sorters, any kind of posting/peg toy. If she finally does attempt them, she will try only a few times, and if she doesn't get it right away, she gets frustrated and moves on to something else." [sr020-0088]

- "Thank you! My mom and MIL wont stop asking me if he’s holding his own bottle yet and it made me nervous that he doesn’t" [sr023-0118]

- "My (almost) 7 month old is zooming around in his walker, whines at us if we don't share our food, sitting up and playing independently for 30 minutes + (supervised). But, he's teething now, and while he chews on his fingers like it's his job he can't figure out how to bring things to his mouth." [sr044-0011]

- "He definitely notices toys and gets excited by them. If I bring a toy up in front of his face, he’ll stare at it, coo at it, kick, move his body and sometimes throw his arms back with excitement, but he doesn’t really move his arms forward towards it to grab it." [sr089-0002]

- "I've been freaking out for a few days because my 3.5 month old never stared at his hands, however began touching his face and sucking his thumb at exactly 3 months. It seems like he just never stared at his hands and will look at a toy in his activity gym and swat at it over and over again like on purpose." [sr049-0097]

**But:** The baby whose parent fears a skipped hand-looking milestone is already interacting with his hands. "I for some reason thought he was just really behind because he never stared at his hands, But he interacts with them fine I guess??" [sr049-0100]

