### The caregiver weighs missing gestures or unusual communication against the child’s other strengths.

13 of 198 posts.

Caregivers describe absent pointing, waving, clapping, imitation or words, inconsistent name response, hand-leading or little interest in other children. Ages are eleven to 20 months, and several ask about autism, a broader developmental profile, or early intervention rather than speech alone. They set concerns beside eye contact, understanding, social games or motor skills; one babysitting relative and one partner describe disagreement about whether assessment is needed.

- "I know autism isn't the end of the world, and I truly respect autistic people and their families. But if I'm being completely honest, I'm grieving the future I imagined for my son, and I'm desperately hoping we're wrong. […] I'm holding onto the smallest bit of hope." [sr050-0030]

