**But:** A later update in one post reports major vocabulary growth while the original pointing concern remains. "Hi! He is still not doing any pointing in the distance, still tip-toe walks, and sometimes gets very absorbed in what he's doing and it can be difficult to get his attention. Besides that everything else seems typical. He doesn't have any sensory issues, has great eye contact and has well over 200 words, sings songs, etc." [sr002-0304]

