**But:** A persistent physical feature can coexist with unaffected breathing and feeding and professional reassurance. "it doesn’t necessarily look large or big. it’s just always out and even sometimes when she’s sleeping. she doesn’t have any difficulty breathing or issues with feeding. the pediatric ENT wasn’t concerned." [sr122-0035]

