**But:** One parent’s loud baby remains happy between episodes, and a feeding change helped discomfort without eliminating loud expression. "In general she is a very happy silly baby, but she has had a ton of belly issues, which I think contributed to her becoming such a grunter. When she was 6 months old we switched from exclusively breastfeeding to mostly giving her a hypoallergenic formula and that has definitely helped with her grunting and discomfort, but she still grunts a lot when she is frustrated or upset and screams instead of cries when she is really upset." [sr062-0088]

