Caregivers connect difficult sleep with learning to roll, stand or walk, becoming more alert, or suddenly using more words. Ages range from 15 weeks to 21 months. They ask whether the new skill or awareness explains the change and describe repeated help settling, holding, transfers or outings that no longer work.

