## Pattern 1, share 05: across the yes posts

All 198 yes posts and 62 near posts were read; none remain unread. Counts describe this assigned share of pattern-1 posts from the random sample, not the prevalence of these situations among parents. Each post is assigned once by its main concern; other concerns can appear in its quotes.

Tags were decided for every post in both sections. “Tried” means an action already taken, including seeking advice, checking information, practising or changing care; plans alone do not count. “Others” means reported words or actions of other people, including partners, relatives, clinicians and commenters; an impersonal milestone chart or an AI answer alone does not count. “Bought” requires an explicit purchase or payment, including payment by insurance; ownership, use, intended purchases and price complaints alone do not count. “Feeling” requires a named feeling or strain, including positive feelings and exhaustion; a question asking whether to worry is not enough by itself. Child feelings alone do not count. Unknown speaker details stay unknown, and quoted medical, vaccine and developmental explanations remain the speakers’ accounts.

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 153 of 198 |
| others | 72 of 198 |
| bought | 3 of 198 |
| feeling | 122 of 198 |

### What they tried, in their words

- "I’ve tried using a push walker and even a walking harness, but she bends her knees within seconds and refuses. She does stand and walk while holding onto furniture (couch, walls) and has been doing that for over a month now. But if I try to hold her hands or fingers to help her walk, she just sits down or bends her knees again." [sr003-0024]

- "We give her a lot of floor time. Place toys a bit far away from her but nothing seems to help or motivate her. Any help or advice is much appreciated as we are first time parents and often times feel guilty that we are not doing everything that we should to help her. We have our checkup coming up with pediatrician in a month but were wondering if we could do something in the meantime to help her." [sr002-0226]

- "I am reading to him a lot, talking to him face to face, playing with him, singing nursery rhymes... nothing seems to be working." [sr034-0048]

- "My son had been so extremely fussy lately that I took him to the pediatrician suspecting he had reflux. We switched to a reflux formula and he’s improved a lot, so I do think we have some reflux stuff going on. He may need baby Pepcid too to help even more — I’m asking his pediatrician about that next week." [sr065-0022]

- "Oh boy, the list of things I've tried for sleep 😅 the list of things I haven't would be shorter, because as far as I can tell, it's only straight cry it out that we've never done. We managed to get about two almost full nights in the crib after a month of Ferber method sleep training, then a road trip set him right back to zero. Now 3 minutes in his crib triggers such hysterics that it takes 20-30 minutes to calm him back down" [sr112-0112]

- "He tries to get into his diaper all day long. We stopped with t shirts and only do onesies. That helped for a bit but now he has learned to pull his pants down and go through the side or undoes the onesie." [sr039-0103]

