- "I try to take his hands out of his mouth as much as I can, but I have 2u2 and lots of times am occupied with my toddler to be consistent with it. I’m worried about it but I feel bad taking away his comfort. I tried a paci or two but prefers the thumb." [sr121-0026]

- "I've tried doing the YouTube thing where you get their head to follow a toy upwards and you help them lift their arm until they fall over. He will track the object, but then gets frustrated or distracted. He still tolerates tummy time if I'm laying flat on my back and he's on my stomach, but even then he's getting frustrated faster than he used to." [sr123-0003]

