# Digest 06: pattern 1, Is this normal, or is something wrong with my child?

Share: baby-development/_work/2026-11/digests/share-06.md. Yes posts: 198. Near posts: 62.

## Pattern 1, share 06: yes posts

### They worry about how their child is learning to hold up their body, roll, crawl or walk.

24 of 198 posts.

These posts ask about weak or wobbly head control, late or inconsistent rolling and sitting, resisting crawling, and taking supported steps without choosing independent walking. The children range from an almost 11-week-old not bringing hands to mouth to an 18-month-old who can walk but still crawls. Parents describe tummy time, exercises, hand support, physiotherapy or medical checks, and comparisons with siblings, twins or other babies; two posts focus on screaming after a new roll.

- "[…] She CAN walk, it’s slow but she can take multiple independent steps. Has been able to for about a month now. However, she is not choosing to walk. She crawls FAST and will walk holding onto something like my finger, the wall, or furniture. But independently she won’t unless we coax her to do it. Sometimes she won’t do it then either, she will just drop and crawl." [sr111-0014]
- "We don’t have to support her head at all when holding or sitting but she will still sometimes kind of throw it around or it’ll drop suddenly! I also feel like when we sit her up support she always looks down and never really straight or up. I’m not sure if I should bring this up to the pediatrician. When we went to our four month appointment, she thought that she would be holding her head completely steady about a week from then, and that was about three weeks ago. She’s definitely able to hold it up, she’s just not 100% sturdy with it and I am worried that she’s not gaining enough neck strength! […]" [sr032-0024]
- "We’ve tried all the pediatric OT tips like kneeling play, putting a toy on the other side of our leg, etc. He wants to hold hands and walk or stand while holding on to things. […]" [sr056-0095]
- "Is there maybe exercises or stretches we need to do to help build up strength or am I just being over cautious and just let the baby be baby and let them do it in their own time-   
Just don't want to be neglectful of not doing something that could be helping them" [sr110-0034]
- "My baby boy is almost 11 weeks old and still doesn’t bring hands to his mouth. He was born full term and good weight, my other two kiddos did it around 8 weeks old or so im getting a little concerned. He smiles and follows with his eyes but i dont see intentions of bringing hands to mouth […]" [sr077-0164]
- "My 3.5 month just learned to roll into her belly. The minute she rolls, she starts crying which quickly escalates to screaming the roof off. I flip her back gently, pick her up, let her be: nothing calms her down!" [sr045-0065]

**But:** Some children already have parts of the skill, and checks have not always found a problem: "She saw a PT about 3 months ago before she was walking and he had no concerns, said it seems like a confidence/balance issue. She had an MRI on her spine and it showed no issues at all. […]" [sr111-0015]

