### They worry because a skill or sound their child used to show has stopped.

7 of 198 posts.

These parents distinguish losing or pausing a previously seen skill from never having reached it: words, gestures, cooing or rolling have stopped. The children range from 20 weeks to 19 months, with several posts about four-to-six-month-old vocal changes. Two parents notice the timing after vaccinations, another wonders about attention shifting to rolling, and toddler parents describe waiting for evaluations or asking whether words are being forgotten.

- "At 15 months she had 8 words. Some of them for quite a while and went with gestures like no or this (shaking head, pointing). Very recently she had started saying Hi Dad, Hi Guys, and Hiya, while waving. That was what I first noticed had stopped. Up until a few days ago when I asked her something she would still shake her head and say No. Now that has stopped. She still says Mama but does not say any other words or the related gestures. Shes gone back to babbling." [sr126-0034]
