- "BUT this last one asked about drawing and using crayons. She still loves ripping up paper and trying to chew on items so like, why would I be giving my child paper and pens, pencils, or crayons... Aren't most toddlers at this age like that??" [sr086-0003]
- "The preschool our 15 month old goes to gave us an ASQ assessment to fill out. It was for 16 months old so one month ahead. He ended up “in the gray area” for most of it and the preschool said they’re not too concerned about it, but will reassess in a couple months. A few things that popped out to me are that he’s not scribbling yet and stacking is something that’s hit or miss as well. There were many places where my spouse and I marked “sometimes” instead of “all the time” because we weren’t 100% on marking either of them." [sr123-0083]

