### They ask what is wrong when their child wakes screaming and cannot settle.

6 of 62 posts.

Parents describe children waking in panic or screaming for hours, needing a bottle or physical contact, or becoming impossible to transfer back to bed. Ages range from 13 months to a child described as two years old. They ask about night terrors, separation, development, pain or medical testing, and describe failed soothing, ear checks, iron supplementation, long waits for specialists and the effect of lost sleep on the family.

- "NOTHING will settle him. We’ve tried milk, food, Calpol, co-sleeping, cuddles, rocking. He just cries and cries basically until he passes out about 4/5am from exhaustion." [sr006-0063]
- "Is it developmental? Is there something wrong with him? This is harder than having a newborn. I am so exhausted and angry and sad." [sr006-0065]
