## Pattern 1, share 06: across the yes posts

| Tag | Posts |
|---|---|
| tried | 158 of 198 |
| others | 105 of 198 |
| bought | 3 of 198 |
| feeling | 131 of 198 |

Each yes post has one main form and a yes/no decision for each tag. Tried includes looking things up, seeking checks, practising skills and changing care; future intentions and passive observation alone do not count. Others includes reported advice, assessments, comments or actions by other adults, including help with care and online information; observing another child's abilities alone does not count. Feeling records the speaker's stated feelings, including curiosity, enjoyment or explicitly not feeling worried; the child's feelings alone do not count. Bought requires an explicit purchase or payment, including a purchase by family.

These are counts of posts in this assigned share of pattern 1 from the random sample of 20,000 posts, not counts of people or estimates of market prevalence. All 198 yes and 62 near posts were read in full as supplied; nothing in the share remains unread. For near posts, unknown ages stay unknown; ages mentioned only as hypothetical examples are not treated as the child's age.

### What they tried, in their words

- "We’ve tried all the pediatric OT tips like kneeling play, putting a toy on the other side of our leg, etc. He wants to hold hands and walk or stand while holding on to things. We recently borrowed a walker from his cousin and he flat out runs in the walker. Like he can seriously zoom around our kitchen to follow our dogs." [sr056-0095]
- "If we try to be interactive with him with mimicking and trying to get him to repeat sounds he looks at us like we are absolutely nuts and has no interest in repeating us." [sr049-0114]
- "I file down her nails as often as I can because she tends to scratch herself, mittens don’t stay on, onesies/long sleeves that fold over her hands she just pokes her fingers through and eventually her whole hand no matter how often you pull the cover back over." [sr066-0033]
- "I’ve been reading her every book about gentle hands and consent, singing songs and frequently reminders that we don’t touch. […]" [sr034-0020]
- "[…] After 3 days post vaccines I slowly started to practice with her rolling over a few times a day.. and by the 7th day she just did it her self. And now she’s fine, back to her normal self." [sr028-0015]
- "I currently have an early intervention appointment to get her evaluated. Did I over reach by referring her to early intervention?" [sr100-0037]
