changes=[
('Parents ask whether movement and practical skills are late.','Head control, walking and hand tasks prompt questions.'),
('Parents question what counts as enough speech.','They ask about babbling, words and combinations.'),
('Parents worry their child does not respond enough.','They watch gestures, smiling and social connection.'),
('Parents ask whether persistent crying will pass.','Clinginess and failed soothing compound uncertainty.'),
('Parents question whether unusual movements signal problems.','Repetition, asymmetry and shaking raise different fears.'),
('Parents question growth, appearance and tooth development.','Size, head shape and tooth timing prompt comparisons.'),
('Parents question too much or too little closeness.','Attachment and stranger distress restrict everyday life.'),
('Parents question normal limits for tantrums and roughness.','They ask about affection, aggression and refusals.'),
('Parents question unusual play, attention and habits.','Questions include activity, preferences and genital exploration.'),
('Parents need clearer expectations of their child.','Readiness, corrected age and milestone definitions confuse.'),
('Parents worry when sounds or skills disappear.','They describe stuttering, stopped gestures and rolling.'),
('Parents want comfort and exploration without injury.','Genital rubbing, sucking and scratching raise boundaries.'),
('Parents seek reassurance while movement skills emerge.','Rolling and falls require rescue or protection.'),
('Parents ask whether fears and sensitivities fade.','Sounds, touch and outings can trigger distress.'),
('Parents question crying during particular care tasks.','Seats, bathing, changes and burping become difficult.'),
('Parents combine observations into wider developmental fears.','Monitoring can take over their interactions.'),
('Parents question loud or unfamiliar vocal sounds.','Screeches and growls bring curiosity or overstimulation.'),
('Parents worry about unusual quietness or alertness.','Calmness and staring can themselves seem alarming.'),
('A parent worries about food spitting and weight loss.','Smaller bites have not solved it.'),
('Parents question whether difficult sleep needs intervention.','Waking, screaming and contact needs prompt troubleshooting.'),
('Parents question how skills and movements affect sleep.','They watch rolling, startling and apparent waking.'),
('Parents question developmental explanations for feeding difficulties.','Refusal, spit-up and changing quantities puzzle them.'),
('Parents worry sleep quantity could harm development.','Both long and short sleep raise questions.'),
('Parents question growth, physical differences and teeth.','Questions include mouth posture and genital variations.'),
('Parents fear injury as mobility develops.','Accounts include rolling fears and confirmed hemorrhage.'),
('Parents question activity, imagination and unusual play.','Comparisons include drawing, attention and body curiosity.'),
('Parents worry about social responses and participation.','Name response, waving and groups prompt questions.'),
('Parents seek explanations for crying and clinginess.','Distress persists despite comfort and medical contact.'),
('Parents question uneven movement and stiffness.','They seek thresholds for concern.'),
('Parents seek boundaries around soothing and body exploration.','Hair pulling, rocking and private-part requests concern them.'),
('Parents seek help with practical and movement skills.','They compare crawling, walking and sock removal.'),
('Parents feel defeated by care and fear failure.','Isolation and unequal care compound developmental worries.'),
('Parents question their child’s memory and emotions.','Fear words, instructions and resumed nursing puzzle.'),
('Parents question ordinary sleep and absent regressions.','One fears delay; another argues for acceptance.'),
('Parents question whether sensory fears need help.','Sounds, mess and personal care remain difficult.'),
('Parents question explanations for tantrums and changed behaviour.','Illness, pinworms and app predictions complicate interpretation.'),
('Parents fear medical events caused unseen brain damage.','They question neonatal crisis or delayed iron treatment.'),
('Parents question whether stooling is still developing.','Grunting and long gaps leave uncertainty.'),
('Parents worry about restricted food and nourishment.','They try alternatives and different offerings.'),
('Parents question speech changes and delay assessments.','They report stuttering or dispute a checkup.'),
('A parent doubts failed hearing and vision screening.','Crying and movement complicate test interpretation.'),
('A parent marvels at functioning on little sleep.','They remain active through a regression.'),
('A parent wants to stop pinching their child.','Exact age: unknown; the share says over 24 months.'),
('Other questions concern clothing, travel, reading and bilingualism.','The bilingual advice remains an unverified claim.'),
('Parents have practised, changed care or sought checks.','Actions include research and booked evaluations.'),
('Other adults leave parents unsure whom to trust.','Clinicians, relatives and caregivers reassure or question.'),
('Few posts explicitly report purchases or paid care.','Includes insurance and an evaluation booked at personal cost.'),
('Parents express fear, guilt, exhaustion, affection and curiosity.','The feeling tag also includes lack of worry.')]
blocks=re.split(r'(?="'^### )'"',body,flags=re.M)
assert len(blocks)-1==len(changes)
for n,(claim,desc) in enumerate(changes,1):
 b=blocks[n]; old=b.splitlines()[0][4:]
